  <title>Bank statement</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Accounting</gui><gui>Bank statement</gui></guiseq> checks a
  bank account's transactions against the statement the bank sends, so the
  books and the bank agree.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Bank Account</gui>. Its balance in the books is
    shown beside it, and every transaction not yet reconciled is
    listed.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click the icon in <gui>Reconcile date</gui> and choose the
    statement's closing date. A date already used for another statement is
    refused.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the bank's closing balance into <gui>Statement
    Balance</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>Reconciled</gui> on each transaction that appears on
    the statement. <gui>Reconciled Balance</gui> and <gui>Difference</gui>
    follow along.</p></item>
    <item><p>When the difference is zero, click <gui>Save reconciled
    items</gui>. Until then the button reads <gui>Reconciled amount does not
    match</gui>, or <gui>No reconcile date</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>Checks are saved as you click them, so a reconciliation can be finished
  later. The checked transactions are only stamped with the reconcile date,
  and leave the list, when they are saved. <gui>Refresh</gui> reloads the
  list. Click a transaction's number, description or date to correct it.</p>

  <section id="missing">
  <title>Transactions the books are missing</title>
  <p>Bank fees and other charges the books do not have yet can be added
  without leaving the window. <gui>Add bank charge</gui> asks for the
  <gui>Amount</gui>, a <gui>Description</gui>, the <gui>Date</gui> and the
  expense account, and posts it. The window menu also opens <link
  xref="double_entry_transaction"/>, <link xref="credit_card_statements">Credit
  card statement</link>, <link xref="incoming_invoice">Incoming
  invoices</link>, <link xref="loan_payment"/> and <link
  xref="miscellaneous_revenue"/>.</p>
  <p><gui>Voided check</gui> in the window menu records a check number that
  was voided: choose the <gui>Bank account</gui>, the <gui>Date</gui> and the
  <gui>Check number</gui>, and click <gui>Apply voided check</gui>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="edit">
  <title>Edit mode</title>
  <p>Check <gui>Edit mode</gui> in the window menu, which asks for the
  administrator password, to right click a transaction and <link
  xref="edit_gl_entry">Edit GL entry</link>.</p>
  </section>

</page>
